From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d8, d3d9: DrawRectPatch, DrawTriPatch, DeletePatch (3682)

d3d8, d3d9: DrawRectPatch, DrawTriPatch, DeletePatch

The three higher-order primitive calls were stubs (DrawRectPatch and
DrawTriPatch reported success without drawing). The control points are read
from stream 0 with the current vertex layout, tessellated on the CPU for
Bezier, uniform B-spline and Catmull-Rom (D3DBASIS_INTERPOLATE) rect patches
of degree 1, 2, 3 and 5 (patch groups of several patches too) and for Bezier
triangle patches, and drawn as an indexed triangle list. Every float, colour
and normalised-integer component of the vertex is evaluated; the stream and
index bindings of the caller are put back afterwards. A patch with a non-zero
handle is remembered and drawn again by a call without a description until
DeletePatch (or a device Reset).
---
